    "submission": "submission-durable.json",
    "summary": "Turn 22 opened a second, independent defect lead — the stable-store metadata record — with a new obligation and its first check.\n\nWhat the source shows. recordInstanceMetadata builds a 9+4N byte buffer and writes the instance's bal at bytes [0:4), then writes vbal at the same [0:4) bytes, then Status at byte [4] and Seq at [5:9), with Deps from offset 9. Two consequences are visible in the source itself: the value written for bal is replaced by vbal, and the Status byte sits inside the four bytes a reader of that field order would use for vbal.\n\nHarness and evidence. The new in-package harness constructs a Replica with Durable true and StableStore pointed at a temp file, records one instance whose bal, vbal, Status and Seq are all distinct, calls the real sync, and reports the produced header verbatim in hex plus flags for which written value appears at offset 0. The local construction run gives header 04030201|03|100f0e0d|deps, i.e. vbal at offset 0, bal absent (bal_field_present false), Status at byte 4 and Seq at [5:9); a prerequisite write-request event carries the instance identity so the header observation is correlated with the write it judges. The formal outcome and a fresh correspondence review are left to the trusted runner.\n\nObligation (new claim C2-durable-record-preserves-written-fields, implementation semantics, priority 1). The requirement is self-consistency of the recorder: each field it writes must be recoverable at the offset where the writer placed it, so no written value is silently replaced by another field of the same record. Its binding locates the recorder (S19-durable-record, symbol recordInstanceMetadata), and the claim's grounding records the derivation, the applicability (Durable true, selectable through epaxos.New), unresolved items (no in-repository reader fixes the intended offsets) and an alternative reading (the record deliberately stores vbal in place of bal) for the reviewer to weigh. Importance is stated narrowly: any reader of the layout would lose the ballot context, but the shipped run.go passes durable=false and no reader exists in the snapshot, so this is an implementation-semantics defect rather than a live availability or agreement failure.\n\nState. The confirmed recovery claim and its three reviewed checks are untouched, the accept-status candidate stays paused with its resume conditions, and no map object, requirement, premise or earlier observation was changed."
